        "answer": {
          "short": "$09\\to81\\to63\\to27\\to45\\to09$.\n\nEvery allowed starting value eventually enters this repeating cycle.",
          "worked": "For example, starting with 21:\n$$\\begin{align*}21-12&=09\\\\90-09&=81\\\\81-18&=63\\\\63-36&=27\\\\72-27&=45\\\\54-45&=09\\end{align*}$$\nThe cycle then repeats. For two unequal digits, their difference is an integer from 1 to 9, so the first result is one of $09,18,27,36,45,54,63,72,81$. Applying the operation to these results leads to the same cycle.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 148
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$n=3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$495$.\n\nEvery allowed starting value eventually reaches 495, which repeats because $954-459=495$.",
          "worked": "Continuing the supplied example:\n$$\\begin{align*}981-189&=792\\\\972-279&=693\\\\963-369&=594\\\\954-459&=495\\\\954-459&=495\\end{align*}$$\nThus 495 is a fixed point. Checking the allowed three-digit starting values gives the same eventual result.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 100
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$n=4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6174$.\n\nEvery allowed starting value eventually reaches 6174, which repeats because $7641-1467=6174$.",
          "worked": "For example, starting with 1234:\n$$\\begin{align*}4321-1234&=3087\\\\8730-0378&=8352\\\\8532-2358&=6174\\\\7641-1467&=6174\\end{align*}$$\nThus 6174 is a fixed point. Checking the allowed four-digit starting values gives the same eventual result.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      }
    ]
  },
